A||||14||dourain86gt||Corvette seats??? Could they... Would they ..... Fit on my fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||dourain86gt||12-03-2001||01:56 AM||||Hey guys I was just wondering if corvette seats would fit in a fiero. I know Trans Am and Camaro seats will fit, but I think with corvette seats I won'y lose as much leg and head room. After all gentlemen and ladies we do drive a tight fitting car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||12-03-2001||02:01 AM||||I asked about this last year... I found a mint set of Black leather seats (1988) in a junkyard.. I think the answer was no...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">       <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red">1984 Indy For Sale ~ <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||Nashco||12-03-2001||02:10 AM||||I think the Fiero seats are very well fitted to the Fiero!  I honestly think they are some of the best bucket seats I've ever seen in a pre-90's car that are made from cloth and have good cloth on them.  My 160k mile car still has no tears in the seats!  If it weren't for the STUPID aftermarket sunroof that somebody put in it, they would be in mint shape.  Unfortunately they've got a slight stain from a drippy roof <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Anyway (sorry to get off topic) are you unsatisfied with your current seats, or are they torn?  You can get some excellent leather seat covers for our seats for a little more than a pair of fair-condition used seats would cost from a junk yard...much cheaper than any leather seats that you could get to fit in the Fiero, I'm sure.  Check them out at <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com" TARGET=_blank>Mr. Mikes</A>.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||dourain86gt||12-03-2001||02:16 AM||||I did check out mr mikes but still too expensive I could get seats from a junkyard from a c-4 corvette for probably around $300. On ebay right know there are seats for $305. These seats are power ones too, and yes my driver side seat has a huge tear in the door side of the seat. not to mention I am sure the cushion is not what it ude to be! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||dourain86gt||12-03-2001||02:17 AM||||Sorry here is the item on ebay <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598596145&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598596145&r=0&t=0</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||12-03-2001||02:32 AM||||Keep in mind that auction still has 3 days left, which means it has the potential of more than doubling in price still!<P>I agree, the padding may be worn after all these years.  My last car was a '69 VW with original seats, so as Jim Carrey said in Me, Myself, and Irene, "My ass has taken a pounding over the years."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||dourain86gt||12-03-2001||02:48 AM||||Any idea on other seats that could work? I plan on changing the interior, too make it look more modern and well new seats may be a way to start?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||12-03-2001||03:17 AM||||Best I could recommend is to go to local junkyards and just start looking around.  Some of them have seats that are already picked and kept out of the weather even.  I got some different seats from a newer vehicle for my VW just by cruising the junkyards.  I wasn't in a hurry, so I checked up on them every couple of weeks.  Eventually you'll find exactly what you're looking for and for the right price, just a matter of looking and waiting.<P>Let us know what you come up with when you do.  I'll be interested to see what fits and stuff.  I plan on putting racing seats in my car, but that kind of info is always fun <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroBUZZ||12-03-2001||11:25 AM||||The real problem in the Fiero is that the spot for your seat is so narrow.  I think a stock seat is like 19".  I was on a search to find something to change the look. LeBaron buckets look classy, Prelude seats will squish in, but they all look large and sit higher off the floor.<P>I rethunk my idea when I went to fetch my GT. 8hour bus ride then drive back home, normally I'd be crippled for days. I arrived fresh as a daisy and in fact I had lunch and went cruising in the new GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>Consider keeping the seats and having them reupolstered in a different pattern or fabric.<P>Gary<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seats.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||kevin||12-03-2001||12:22 PM||||Haze,<BR>I missed your question last year on the possibility of putting in Corvette seats in a Fiero. YOu say they do not fit? Why? Was there clearance problems? Was it becasue the mounting holes were not compatible? What were the details. Did you actually do a dry fit? Let me know. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChopTop||12-03-2001||02:23 PM||||I have a pair of red leather seats from a 1980 corvette (clamshell style).  I pulled the Fiero seats out one day and set them in, they looked great and fit fine.  The problem is you have to modify seat tracks in order to use them.||||reg||1
Z||000011||dourain86gt||12-03-2001||04:40 PM||||Hey fierobuzz, what seats are those in that pic there? tjose look pretty good! Is that your fiero?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000012||Alex4mula||12-03-2001||06:06 PM||||C5 seats will fit perfectly in terms of size. I used to have ones and measured them. Track rails is another thing. Basicaly you will need to adapt Fiero rails to the Vette seats.||||reg||1
Z||000013||dourain86gt||12-04-2001||12:56 AM||||C5 seats! Wow wouldn't that be great! But i am sure those seats would probably be more expensive then the best Recaros! But who knows wha the cards may lay a C5 could be in junk yard tomorow and amazingly the owner of the junk yard doesn't know there real worth and I could gte them for under $1000. I wish but too expensive. Nice to know though thanks!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
